id: pm-jira-adf-block-evidence
title: Capture selected structured Jira description blocks as portable evidence
description: ""
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T03:46:37.895Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T05:29:35.781Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Table cell and code block round-trip with stable source coordinates; unsupported nodes are counted; changed source revision refuses approved capture.
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T03:47:27.247Z",codex-agent,"Design: portable read-only capture packets preserve original RFC 6901 coordinates and ancestor scaffolding, never pull attachments or mutate native items. Approval compares both the caller-provided source revision and complete description digest, catching same-revision edits as well. Replay validates the exact producer schema and digest. No transaction isolation or remote freshness claim: callers supply a newly read source snapshot; this feature has no target writes, leases or frozen journal. Existing atomic replay work remains tracked separately by pm-jira-atomic-replay-revisions."
  "2026-10-29T03:53:18.949Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed captureAdfEvidence/replayAdfEvidence plus jira capture-adf, with strict shared node schema, original JSON pointers, ancestor scaffolding, immutable copied attributes, digest/revision approval, complete exclusion counts and all-or-refuse output bounds. Added documented example and pm-evidence citation handoff. Seeded 500-sequence selection/approval property passed; native import/export/sync reference-model coverage now also asserts capture/replay against exact SDK readback. Targeted malformed-schema, sparse-array, CRLF, foreign packet and non-git CLI checks are in progress."
  "2026-10-29T03:58:20.664Z",codex-agent,"Real-data measurement used a read-only, non-git copy of public main at eaeaf48: 112 native items; exact SDK-read title/body-or-description projected into ADF table/code wrappers; 112 captures and round trips; 112 changed-revision refusals; 1680 source nodes, 560 retained nodes; 14825 native body bytes; 200704 emitted bytes, maximum packet 3996 bytes; zero budget refusals, zero Jira calls and unchanged SDK native state. This is real public tracker content in explicit ADF projections, not a live Jira validation."
  "2026-10-29T04:02:43.861Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: disposable non-git copies with only the source-revision guard disabled or original coordinates discarded both fail the table/code regression; the unchanged fixed implementation then passes. Pinned pm test --run --progress passed 9/9 focused tests with no skips. Typecheck, test compilation and docstrings pass. Full npm/Bun release checks remain assigned to CI at unchanged thresholds. Local health initially reports extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew in the preinstalled pm-github graph; refreshing the ignored project extension using the CI installation contract."
  "2026-10-29T04:03:51.238Z",codex-agent,"Focused coverage reports 100% lines, branches and functions in both new feature modules. All six real packed launch/install modes passed on host 2026.10.28 (24 mode assertions, one artifact): npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx, npm local and Bun local. Local strict tracker health now passes after refreshing pm-github exactly as CI does; only its ignored install graph changed and the managed registry timestamp was restored. Final packet-domain hardening narrows pointer indices and count bounds to producer domains; final exact-artifact acceptance will repeat after final generation."
  "2026-10-29T04:06:17.247Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jira/pull/178 . Implementation commit d5fc6d8. Final source-domain hardening passes 7/7 core tests with 100% lines/branches/functions; installed no-git command previously passed 2/2, combined focused suite 9/9. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun release gates are running in the PR Node 22/26 CI matrix; exact-head evidence will be reported in the PR and handoff. Final generated-artifact acceptance is repeating all six installation modes. Existing atomic-import replay revision and interruption limitations remain out of this read-only feature scope and already have tracker items. No new SDK gap was encountered."
  "2026-10-29T04:12:11.795Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI at f0b2693 passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jira/actions/runs/40815913116 . Node 22 and 26 each passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check: 310/310 tests per gate, zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions across all 9 measured source files. Model diagnostics confirm 500 native sequences plus 2000 evidence operations and 40 safely refused older atomic replays. Final package SHA-256 9a37c667dda80f225b8761f7090cc6de183833780a2426ea0a9660a268bb5b45 passed all six install modes / 24 assertions. DeepScan identified one low-impact validation-script issue: an array used only as a counter. Replaced it with a numeric counter; production artifact bytes are unaffected. Final fresh CI will verify the follow-up head. Automated review availability: Sourcery/cubic quota-limited, Greptile trial ended, CodeRabbit skipped; these are not approvals."
  "2026-10-29T04:15:09.387Z",codex-agent,"Final official-ADF schema check identified a must-allow compatibility case: codeBlock may carry an empty marks array and block nodes may carry formatting marks. Widened only the new source boundary to accept bounded mark arrays on blocks; producers still discard block formatting and count omitted marks, and retained packets still disallow block marks. Added must-allow producer/replay regression including table-cell paragraph alignment and empty code-block marks. This preserves structure without exporting unwanted formatting data. Final artifact/CI acceptance will repeat for this source compatibility change."
  "2026-10-29T04:34:36.503Z",codex-agent,"Bounded CI handoff: after the queue-rules wait window, final source head f1321a7 still has Node 22/26 CI queued with no started steps: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jira/actions/runs/40816747611 ; CodeQL is also queued: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jira/actions/runs/40816747624 . Do not treat these as passing evidence. Earlier source head f0b2693 passed all four npm/Bun release gates with 310/310 tests each, zero skips/failures and 100% lines/branches/functions across 9 sources (run 40815913116). Final compatibility source passed 7/7 core tests at 100% coverage; all six actual packed install modes passed 24 mode assertions on immutable artifact SHA-256 c7a209d6e3092753abc9c087ca820fb488048c9ff16ad081df59085ad9f44d9b (45 files). Repeated final-source read-only public tracker validation again passed all 112 captures/round trips and 112 changed-revision refusals with unchanged native state; measured bytes/nodes remain identical. The compatibility behavioral revert also fails as required in a disposable copy. Canceled only the superseded queued CI run 40816453498. Automated reviewer quota/skip receipts remain missing approvals. This final tracker-only commit will also require exact-head CI; item stays in_progress and unclaimed for orchestrator verification. No merge/release performed; no new SDK gap encountered."
  "2026-10-29T04:53:39.305Z",codex-agent,"Re-review class: remote compatibility and producer/validator agreement. Valid editor defaults must remain readable across both tableCell and tableHeader, selected and unselected source nodes, preview/approved capture and packet replay. Whole-package search found one shared attribute validator used by these paths; legacy adfToPlainText ignores attributes. Checking all recognized optional defaults, JSON/TOON adapters, packed npm/Bun consumers and non-git SDK readback. Branch is current with origin/main; no merge needed. Supplied review has one blocking finding; GitHub inline comments contain no additional findings."
  "2026-10-29T04:59:19.681Z",codex-agent,"Class closure: all recognized nullable editor defaults now share one source/packet rule: tableCell/tableHeader colwidth and background, plus codeBlock language. Confirmed from published Atlassian adf-schema 57.7.26 tableNodes and generated nodeTypes (https://www.npmjs.com/package/@atlaskit/adf-schema/v/57.7.26). Other retained numeric defaults remain non-null; unfamiliar optional attrs stay source-only. New 500-sequence property covers both cell kinds, omitted/null/explicit values, selected/unselected/context cells, source coordinates, CRLF and stale approvals. Must-refuse corpus checks malformed attrs both in full sources and re-signed packets. Behavioral revert proof in disposable non-git copies: reverting only validAttrs, or individually rejecting null colwidth, background or language, makes the new property fail with invalid_input (exit 1); must-refuse corpus still passes. Fixed focused tests pass 11/11; typecheck, test typecheck and docstring gate pass. JSON/TOON round-trip uses SDK decodePmTableRows receipts, never a handwritten normalizer. Native 500-sequence model now includes selected/unselected nullable table defaults read from real SDK state."
  "2026-10-29T05:05:18.913Z",codex-agent,"Verification update: focused linked tests passed 11/11 and static gates passed. The native model hit the linked runner default 120-second timeout without an assertion failure; retry uses the supported runtime --timeout 900 override. Persisting timeout_seconds metadata was safely refused by the project runtime floor, so no pins or item-format migration were changed. The failed run is retained in the work record. Public read-only non-git validation with nullable defaults: 112 items/captures/round trips/revision refusals, 1680 source nodes, 560 retained nodes, 14825 native body bytes, 216832 emitted bytes, maximum 4140 bytes, zero budget refusals, native state changes or live Jira calls. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun release gates remain assigned to CI, two workers per suite, under the shared-host rule."
  "2026-10-29T05:12:11.294Z",codex-agent,"Packed harness correction: npm-global and bun-global passed both selection profiles. The newly added standalone SDK replay consumer then failed on the raw npx artifact extraction because that extraction had no installed peer SDK; host capture itself had passed. The harness now installs the declared peer explicitly for raw extracted SDK consumers, using ordinary package resolution and the supported loader, without production changes or argv/symlink path discovery. Retrying all six modes on one immutable artifact; no SDK gap is claimed."
  "2026-10-29T05:16:48.030Z",codex-agent,"Bounded native-model retry passed: pm test pm-jira-adf-block-evidence --run --only-index 4 --timeout 900 --progress. One test, 500 random sequences, 2000 native operations plus 2000 evidence operations, 40 safely refused older atomic replays, zero failures or skips; complete target/reference states read back through the SDK match. Runtime was about 696 seconds on the shared host. First default-timeout attempt remains documented. Nullable defaults, source-coordinate replay and native relationships are all covered without reducing the sequence count or weakening existing tests."
  "2026-10-29T05:29:31.596Z",codex-agent,"Final local evidence for re-review: all six packed modes passed (npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx, npm local, Bun local), 108 scenario assertions, host 2026.10.28, one immutable 45-file artifact SHA-256 216af8092c0a56cc60af4d2b27862d925930d4e3fe11095f953117a16e9c80fc. Both selected cells/header/code and code-only captures beside unselected null-default tables preserve JSON/TOON and SDK replay. The harness installs the declared peer for raw SDK consumers. Four behavioral reverts still fail the final exact-attribute property; fixed properties pass 2/2 afterward. Focused tests 11/11, native model 500 sequences with 2000 native plus 2000 evidence operations, typecheck, build:test, docstring (20 files/99 declarations), strict health, privacy scan and append-only history checks pass. Latest origin/main is already an ancestor. No tests were deleted or weakened. Full npm/Bun release gates will run on the final pushed head in CI, two workers per suite; the PR will carry exact run URLs and counts. Only supplied blocking class and its related nullable defaults required production changes; no other review findings were available. Remaining boundary: offline snapshots cannot observe edits after the caller last read the source. No new SDK gap; timeout metadata compatibility refusal is documented with its runtime override remedy."
